    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0591" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/15716½: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Windsor, Vt.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[Received 4:20 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I do not see why Villa’s arbitrary actions should in any way interfere with the
                    success of the conference now being held. The object of that conference is to
                    advise as to the best methods of handling just such matters after a plan has
                    been agreed upon by which the various leaders are to be informed of what they
                    are to expect from the United States and what it will be possible and impossible
                    for them to accomplish if they resist the purposes expressed by the
                    conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
